{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt'","aggregated_output":"     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/*.diff'","aggregated_output":"--- blind_adjudicate.py\t2026-11-22 19:58:24\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/blind_adjudicate.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:54\n@@ -23,8 +23,8 @@\n - part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n   includes it.\n - two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n-  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n-  calculation (a ruling).\n+  guidance and used as a stated benchmark for an estimate, or applied (apply_growth) to a base built on the quarter's one forecast\n+  figure, is not a second value, when that figure supplies the quarter's value in the calculation (a ruling).\n - own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n   estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n   applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n--- blind_test.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:05\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/blind_test.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:54\n@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n \n HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\n@@ -173,8 +173,8 @@\n - part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n   includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\n - two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n-  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n-  calculation (a ruling).\n+  guidance and used as a stated benchmark for an estimate, or applied (apply_growth) to a base built on the quarter's one forecast\n+  figure, is not a second value, when that figure supplies the quarter's value in the calculation (a ruling).\n - own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n   estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n   applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n--- calc_small.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:05\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/calc_small.py\t2026-11-22 20:10:43\n@@ -612,6 +612,18 @@\n     return tops\n \n \n+def _beneath_inputs(figs, fid):\n+    \"\"\"The figure and every figure it is computed from, along inputs.\"\"\"\n+    found, stack = set(), [fid]\n+    while stack:\n+        g = stack.pop()\n+        if g in found or g not in figs:\n+            continue\n+        found.add(g)\n+        stack.extend(figs[g].get('inputs') or [])\n+    return found\n+\n+\n def _shared(family, figs, outcomes):\n     errors = []\n     by_key = {}\n@@ -640,7 +652,10 @@\n                     reached.append(fid)\n                     if f['basis'] == 'forecast':\n                         continue                           # through the forecast figure: what lies beneath it is its basis\n-                stack.extend(f.get('inputs') or [])\n+                ins = list(f.get('inputs') or [])\n+                if f.get('operation') == 'apply_growth' and len(ins) == 2 and len(node) == 1 and node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0]):\n+                    ins = ins[:1]                          # [D742] a rate applied to this quarter's forecast is a benchmark (D741 ruling 1)\n+                stack.extend(ins)\n             if not reached:\n                 continue\n             if len(node) != 1:\n--- render_v13.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:05\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/render_v13.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:54\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n \n HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n import calc_check as cc  # noqa: E402\n@@ -151,7 +151,8 @@\n     })\n     return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure, 'description': 'The family\\'s calculation. Use one forecast figure for each '\n                             'quantity and period, as a point or a range, wherever that quantity is needed (outside figures beneath it, or a '\n-                            'point a final range rests on, are fine). A growth rate computed from guidance may serve as a stated benchmark for an estimate. '\n+                            'point a final range rests on, are fine). A growth rate computed from guidance may serve as a stated benchmark for an estimate, '\n+                            'or be applied with apply_growth to a base built on your forecast figure. '\n                             'To turn a total into a narrower quantity (data-center spending out of total capital expenditure), write the '\n                             'deduction or share as its own figure, or give a supported bound; never relabel a total as the narrower quantity. '\n                             'Figures name each other by id; no figure may depend on itself.'},\n@@ -174,7 +175,8 @@\n                      'never adds the part into the whole for the same period; a difference may take the part from the whole of the same '\n                      'period only to give the rest.')\n     shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family.get('shared', [])) or 'none'\n-    lines.append(f'Shared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: {shared}.')\n+    lines.append(f'Shared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes '\n+                 f'(a growth rate applied with apply_growth to a base built on that forecast is the one exception): {shared}.')\n     keys = '; '.join(f'{v} = {m[\"what\"][\"population\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"measure\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"scope\"]} | {m[\"what\"][\"period\"]}'\n                      + (f' ({m[\"key_note\"]})' if m.get('key_note') else '') for v, m in family.get('members', {}).items() if v in shown)\n     lines.append(f'Outcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: {keys}.')\n--- small_cases.py\t2026-11-22 19:43:03\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/small_cases.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:04\n@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n \n HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n if os.environ.get('CALC_SMALL_DIR'):                     # small_mutants.py: a mutated calc_small.py on a scratch copy\n@@ -356,6 +356,26 @@\n def _():\n     a = base_pair()\n     a['figures'].append(F('REST', W('other', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=30.375, inputs=['F6', 'F12'], operation='difference'))\n+    return a, PAIR\n+\n+\n+@case('A1', 'a guidance-implied growth rate applied to the Q3 forecast for Q4 (D741 ruling 1) [D742]', 'pass')\n+def _():\n+    a = base_pair()\n+    a['figures'].append(F('G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue sequential growth'), 'computed', 'guidance', '%', value=12.27, inputs=['F2', 'F3'], operation='growth'))\n+    fig(a, 'F5').update(kind='computed', basis_text=None, rests_on=None, inputs=['F4', 'G'], operation='apply_growth', value=123.49)\n+    fig(a, 'F6').update(value=411.29)\n+    fig(a, 'F11').update(value=114.23)\n+    fig(a, 'F12').update(value=380.28)\n+    return a, PAIR\n+\n+\n+@case('A1', 'the Data Center Q3 forecast grown at the guided company rate for Q4 (D741 ruling 1) [D742]', 'pass')\n+def _():\n+    a = base_pair()\n+    a['figures'].append(F('G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue sequential growth'), 'computed', 'guidance', '%', value=12.27, inputs=['F2', 'F3'], operation='growth'))\n+    fig(a, 'F11').update(inputs=['F10', 'G'], operation='apply_growth', value=114.23)\n+    fig(a, 'F12').update(value=380.28)\n     return a, PAIR\n \n \n@@ -391,6 +411,20 @@\n defect('an unused second forecast of a quarter is not counted (passes)', 'pass', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n     'ALT', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=112.0, basis_text='an alternative not used')))\n defect('Q3 guidance used directly beside the Q3 forecast (S4)', 'S4', lambda a: fig(a, 'F10').update(inputs=['F3', 'F9'], value=99.9))\n+defect('the guided Q2-to-Q3 rate applied to Q2 rebuilds a Q3 value beside the forecast (S4) [D742]', 'S4', lambda a: (a['figures'].extend([\n+    F('G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue sequential growth'), 'computed', 'guidance', '%', value=12.27, inputs=['F2', 'F3'], operation='growth'),\n+    F('Q3B', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'computed', 'guidance', 'USD bn', value=108.0, inputs=['F2', 'G'], operation='apply_growth')]),\n+    fig(a, 'F10').update(inputs=['Q3B', 'F9'], value=99.9), fig(a, 'F12').update(value=370.575)))\n+MESSAGES['the guided Q2-to-Q3 rate applied to Q2 rebuilds a Q3 value beside the forecast (S4) [D742]'] = 'Q3B for NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027 Q3'\n+defect('Q4 built on the guided Q3 through the guided multiple applied twice to Q2 (S4) [D742]', 'S4', lambda a: (a['figures'].append(\n+    F('X', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue sequential multiple'), 'computed', 'guidance', 'x', value=1.1227, inputs=['F3', 'F2'], operation='ratio')),\n+    fig(a, 'F5').update(kind='computed', basis_text=None, rests_on=None, inputs=['F2', 'X', 'X'], operation='product', value=121.25),\n+    fig(a, 'F6').update(value=409.05), fig(a, 'F11').update(value=112.16), fig(a, 'F12').update(value=378.21)))\n+defect('Q4 grown from a run-rate rebuilt from Q2 at the guided rate, not from the Q3 forecast (S4) [D742]', 'S4', lambda a: (a['figures'].extend([\n+    F('G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue sequential growth'), 'computed', 'guidance', '%', value=12.27, inputs=['F2', 'F3'], operation='growth'),\n+    F('T', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3', measure='revenue run-rate'), 'computed', 'guidance', 'USD bn', value=108.0, inputs=['F2', 'G'], operation='apply_growth')]),\n+    fig(a, 'F5').update(kind='computed', basis_text=None, rests_on=None, inputs=['T', 'G'], operation='apply_growth', value=121.25),\n+    fig(a, 'F6').update(value=409.05), fig(a, 'F11').update(value=112.16), fig(a, 'F12').update(value=378.21)))\n defect('two Data Center Q4 forecasts, both used (S4)', 'S4', lambda a: (a['figures'].append(F(\n     'BAD', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=104.0, basis_text='another view')),\n     fig(a, 'F12').update(outcome_for=[]), a['figures'].append(F('X', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=372.0,\n--- small_mutants.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:29\n+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/small_mutants.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:04\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n from pathlib import Path\n \n HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n M = [\n     ('S1 value', \"            ok = _same(f.get('value'), parsed['value'])\\n\", \"            ok = True\\n\"),\n     ('S1 qualifier', \"        if q not in written:\\n\", \"        if False:\\n\"),\n@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@\n     ('S4 two forecasts', \"        if len(ids) > 1:\\n            errors.append(('S4'\", \"        if False:\\n            errors.append(('S4'\"),\n     ('S4 adopted only', \"        if k not in keys:\\n            tops.add(fid)\", \"        if True:\\n            tops.add(fid)\"),\n     ('S4 bypass', \"            if bypass:\\n\", \"            if False:\\n\"),\n+    ('S4 benchmark exemption [D742]', \"and node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0]):\", \"and False:\"),\n+    ('S4 exemption needs the forecast as base [D742]', \"and node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0]):\", \":\"),\n     ('S5 estimate under reference', \"            if any(figs[g]['kind'] == 'estimate' for g in chain):\", \"            if False:\"),\n     ('S5 forecast under reference', \"            elif any(figs[g]['basis'] == 'forecast' for g in chain):\", \"            elif False:\"),\n     ('S5 outside source', \"            elif not any(figs[g]['kind'] == 'source' and figs[g]['basis'] in EXTERNAL for g in chain):\", \"            elif False:\"),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '430,490p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"\nThe council's reversible decisions on Alex's page are recorded in D606 and D607.\n\n**The merge test (D678–D680, 2026-11-19): closed; the registered test did not pass.** The old system opens questions, clean Step 1 reads\nand files under them, and the frozen judge answers. It ran on 70 articles × old-2 and old-3, with a hybrid arm and a control arm, for\n$2.13 ([result](research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md)).\n- **Held:**\n  - delivery: the decisive statements reached the judge on 4/4 primary questions in both draws;\n  - talks stayed talks;\n  - both blind readers supported all 4 hybrid answers;\n  - no five-company or 2027 figure was taken as the answer;\n  - c8 proposed no NVIDIA-figure question.\n- **Missed:**\n  - P2's proxy clause: total capex is used for data-center capex without being named a proxy, which old also misses;\n  - V: the rebuilt control's v47 was unsupported, and a reconstruction effect is not ruled out.\n- **Not shown:** that the merge answers better. The old answers were already supported, and the capex band was set by 09-06 history.\n- **Next:** superseded by D681, below.\n\n**The one next task: re-run the v13s blind test once with fresh writers and readers, after the reader calibration on Alex's rulings (D740, D741).**\n\n- **The first blind test stopped** (D740, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md`):\n  - 12 of 12 first answers were schema-valid, and 11 of 12 passed every check.\n  - **Stop 1:** S1 read \"from $35 billion to $170 billion\" as a range. This was Claude's change, now fixed: an \"X to Y\" after \"from\" is a\n    change between two values.\n  - **Stop 2:** the readers marked a guidance-implied growth benchmark as \"two forecasts of one quarter\".\n- **Alex ruled the readers' boundary questions** (D741):\n  - a guidance-implied growth benchmark is not a defect;\n  - consensus total × a past quarter's share is not the market's reference, and S5 now refuses it;\n  - a total used for a narrower quantity must state its deduction or a supported bound.\n- **Checks:** cases 104 of 104, mutants 40 of 40, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the old harness unchanged.\n- **The reader calibration on six stored boundary replies** (`calibration-D741/`) runs before the re-run.\n- **A clean re-run** goes to Alex as the paid re-send request.\n\nThe record before D740:\n\n- **The format shrank** (D737). Alex chose to shrink it after round 51 (D736) found the full restatement unbounded.\n- **What code refuses** (D738): only the five named defects, where the calculation's own structure decides them, plus broken\n  structure. Indirect forms are recorded for readers.\n- **The small format is built and rehearsed at $0** (D739):\n  - `calc_small.py`, the v13s schema and header, and format selection in `paid_gate.py`;\n  - cases 100 of 100, mutants 38 of 38, rehearsal 19 of 19;\n  - the old harness unchanged.\n- **The blind test** (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5): six registered requests, each written by a fresh Claude subagent and a fresh read-only\n  Codex session, in `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/`. Two readers then grade every reply. A clean result goes to Alex as the\n  request for the paid re-send. Nothing paid is sent before that.\n\nThe record before D737 (superseded as the next task):\n\n**Earlier next task: finish judging-v13's repair to the council's line, then run the $0 blind test (D734, D735).**\n\n- **Alex chose the repair** (D734; his words are in the decision log).\n- **Round 51 (D736)** found as many serious issues in design v2 as round 49 found in v1. Codex would fix them and use the last\n  round; Claude would go back to Alex now. The choice is with Alex.\n- **The finish line (council rounds 49–50, D735):**\n  - at most two more review rounds: round 51 on the exact wording and cases (`REPAIR-DESIGN.md` v2), then one on the request the\n    harness actually sends and its checks;\n  - then the blind test once, as `REPAIR-DESIGN.md` §5 registers it;\n  - a serious issue left after the second round goes back to Alex.\n- **A clean blind test** returns to Alex as a request for the paid re-send.\n- **Nothing paid is sent before that.**\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '11300,11445p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"  - **S8:**\n    - a correct sum of the part and the whole for different periods was refused;\n    - a remainder across periods was accepted;\n    - a period added twice was accepted.\n  - **S4:** an unused or superseded figure was counted. Only the forecasts the outcomes adopt now count.\n  - **S5/S7:** `rests_on` is enforced for estimates only and `inputs` for computed figures only, and numbers must be finite.\n  - **The runner:** it now refuses a reply that is not exactly one JSON object, an incomplete inventory, and a ladder out of order.\n    A checker error is recorded per reply.\n- **Checks:**\n  - `small_cases.py`: 100 of 100, each an exact rule set;\n  - `small_mutants.py`: 38 mutants caught, and the control passes;\n  - `small_rehearsal.py`: 19 of 19, including a defective and a correct answer for each named defect through the gate path, and the old\n    run reproduced byte for byte;\n  - the old harness unchanged: rehearsal 63 of 63, the $0 gate 87 of 87, the old plan's bytes identical.\n- **Size:**\n  - The v13s schema is about 14,300 characters against about 9,600, and a whole pair request about 140,000 characters against\n    134,000. It is larger, not smaller as SMALL-DESIGN.md §4 expected.\n  - The reason: the fields the old request left undefined now carry their rules (AGENTS §6).\n- **Decided:**\n  - The blind test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5) runs now, without a further design round. It costs $0 at the provider.\n  - Its stop conditions measure the same classes empirically: readers mark the five defects on every reply, and an accepted reply with\n    a marked defect stops the test.\n  - Its result goes to a council round (Council B) before anything goes to Alex.\n- **Output:** `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/`.\n\n## D740 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s blind test stops on a checker error and a reader-marked defect; council round 55 sends three reader rulings to Alex\n\n- **Result** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22/`; $0 at the\n  provider):\n  - All 12 first answers (six cases, Claude and Codex writers) were schema-valid, and 11 passed every check.\n  - **Stop 1:** S1 refused a right answer. \"From $35 billion to $170 billion\" was read as a range, through round 54's \"to\" range form\n    (Claude's mistake). The old checker had excluded that form for exactly this ambiguity.\n  - **Stop 2:** both readers and both adjudicators marked R06, a guidance-implied Q3 growth benchmark used while forecasting Q3 above\n    guidance, as \"two forecasts of one quarter\". Both adjudicators rejected R12's claim, which has the same pattern.\n  - The reader families split on a computed market reference (consensus total × last quarter's segment share; R02, R05, R08, R12) and\n    on total capex used as data-center capex (R09).\n- **Council round 55** (`codex-r55.md`):\n  - STOP is correct as registered, and the counts reconcile (three wordings corrected).\n  - R06 and R12 are the same method, so the readers' boundary is unstable.\n  - The three rulings go to Alex.\n  - **Next:**\n    - fix the S1 range;\n    - apply the rulings, in the reader brief and in code only where the structure decides them;\n    - verify both reader families on the stored boundary replies;\n    - re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers, then the paid re-send request.\n\n## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n\n- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n- **How they are applied (D738):**\n  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n  - Then three steps:\n    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 13 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md'","aggregated_output":"| 29 | 11-05 凌晨 | 独立读者核对结果、挑战\"直接做进生产再跑 14 天\"的建议 | 判断理由站得住、记录如实（发之前的版本已还原、锁定码对上）；但只测了 2/22 道题，财报里有挨着但不是那个量的数（v20、v9 旁边），而冻结版本已判对 15–16 道；文件是人挑的；\"和存档比\"违反 PRD 10 | 建议撤回；下一步：同样的读法用在全部 22 道种子题，读到数的题在窗口末判断、当天重发对照，已判对的题一道不能变错 |\n| 30 | 11-05 | Alex：\"你充分验证\"。乙的全部 22 道题验证：设计（`baseline-design.md` 第 8 轮）——文件由代码选（开始跟踪前最近一个财报日的财报类材料：5 月 20 日新闻稿和 CFO 说明）；读法和第二版一字不差，每题每份文件 3 次；判断照 PRD 10 §4 当天原样重发：三遍各自拿窗口末最后一次判断的存档请求，对照原样 3 次，起点组只在证据块最前面加上读到的数；过关三条事先写下（v10、v12 各 ≥ 6/9；不弄坏：同一遍里重排的精确检验显著少、或少 2 次以上且两人读理由认定是起点数带偏；读到的数五类分类，读错、别的量、不是数一个都不能有） | 发之前修了两处：读法的检查原来要求\"引用的最后一个数就是读到的数\"，照抄整句的正常引用会被拒（4 句全拒），改成\"读到的数印在引用里\"（对照 32 例全对，两个弄坏的版本分别抓出 5、1 个错；试点重放只有 v10 第 3 次那两条整行变成收下，v10 变 3/3）；发送脚本按冻结尺子补上是非题判法、\"档动了\"对着请求里那次上一次结论查（三遍存档 57 个结论和 `score_judgement.py` 逐题一致，弄坏的判法被抓出）。审查：Codex 4 轮（第 1 轮 5 条严重、第 2 轮 3 条严重，都属实都改；第 3、4 轮无严重问题），独立读者 1 次（请求干净、没有金标泄漏；挪档看不见、单位后缀、口径错等照改） | 设计和 8 个脚本锁定（`baseline-all.sha256`）；发读数 132 次 |\n| 31 | 11-05 | 乙的全部 22 道题验证，照锁定的设计测一次：读 132 次（0.083 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、判断 144 次（0.344 美元），三遍各自和当天原样重发的对照比 | **第 1 条过**：v10、v12 各 9/9 判对。**第 2 条过**：读到数的 7 道判过的题两组选档逐次一样，只有 v22 第 2 遍少 1 次（7/9 对 6/9，理由显示是本来的抽样起伏，起点组写明\"没有把一季度乘 4\"）。**第 3 条没过**：53 个收下的数里 5 个是别的量——v19（Vera CPU 收入）两次收了\"数据中心计算收入 604 亿\"，v20（Blackwell 和 Rubin 收入）两次收了\"数据中心收入 752 亿\"和\"网络收入 148 亿\"；判断都没被带偏（v19 理由写明计算收入里没有单列 Vera CPU） | 照登记停，交 Alex |\n| 32 | 11-05 | 问模型自己为什么收那 5 个数（3 次，约 0.3 美分，`probe-baseline-account.md`） | 3 次都指向读法任务里那一句\"报告没用题目的名字写这个量时，写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"，并自己说这些数不是这道题的量、不该写。这一句是 v10、v12 要用的，在报告根本没有这个量的题上把模型推去写更大或旁边的行 | 建议：只改这一句的边界（只收\"由它算出的那几行\"和\"换了名字的同一个量\"，更大的、旁边的行不算），按提示词审计改，再在 22 道题上测一次；等 Alex 的话 |\n| 33 | 11-05 | Alex：\"改\"。只改读法里那一句：原句\"写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"→ 新句\"只写算出它的那几行，或换了名字的同一个量；更大的行、旁边的行都不写\"（任务 790 → 889 字符，理由：抽象说法换成闭合两类加边界）。提示词审计、Codex 只读审 1 轮（1 条严重：发送失败会被当成白卷，已改成\"不完整、不下结论\"）；先在 v19、v20、v10、v12 上试