{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D742|r56b|reflection|another quantity' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers docs/DECISIONS-log.md -g '*.md' -g '*.py' -g '*.txt' -g '\"'!s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2960:  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, \"A\"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 \"another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)\" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3001:- Alex, after the end-to-end measurement and the reflection (`research/2026-10-31-reference-context/design-e2e.md`, `reflection-2026-10-31.md`: the placement call drops a third of the extracted core matters and 70% of the supporting ones for want of a question to file them under, while the questions those statements name — demand, inputs, competition and share, pricing, the company's own annual lines — are the root quantities and seven driver classes D208 designed and marked not built): the seed list for NVDA was put to him as a table (roots: FY2027 total revenue, data-center revenue, non-GAAP gross margin; drivers: hyperscaler capex 2026, server-memory contract price 2027, NVIDIA's share of 2026 data-center accelerator spending, the Rubin rack's price, Rubin shipping, China's H200 permission, AI Compute Partnership commitments). Alex: \"可以吧\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3852:- Alex, on Claude's report of the three-round reflection with Codex (`docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/reflection-v74l.md`), which\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4544:- **Decided:** after each round of work (a probe, a measurement, a change of design), Claude writes its own reflection, has the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4549:- **Done on the day:** written into AGENTS §7.3 at the council rule, in his words; a reflection council on the whole Step 4\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4893:- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mk-*`): Claude's reflection written first (`mk-my-reflection.md`); an independent Codex member investigated cold and reached the same recommendation (`mk-codex.md`: \"Run the bounded D431 comparison as a diagnostic, then choose the repair from the final-answer losses\"), correcting two of Claude's statements (the comparison does not by itself identify the largest cause; Stage B also missed its last-judgement line on the strictest reading). Consensus: \"Council position: consensus on the next step in mk-challenge-1.md\" (`mk-codex-2.md`).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5033:  reviewed by the council before the trial, the trial, the reading; (3) then a reflection on one next angle: how a source becomes a question\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5045:  the reflection on how sources become questions.\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5048:  stored Stage B missed its last-judgement line on its strictest reading). Next: the reflection on how a source becomes a question with the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5232:  The next direction comes from the deep reflection council Alex asked for.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5234:## D466 · 2026-11-13 · Deep reflection (Alex's request): stop circling, two choices for Alex, one in-scope measurement prepared at $0, new guard lines (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5257:  what was read first-hand; two falsified or error-moving angles in a row trigger a reflection council (or Alex, when active) before any next\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5465:## D483 · 2026-11-14 · Deep reflection council (mw): the way to production 