- Run folder: `poc/data/clean-deepseek-probe-2026-11-17/run-1`; result: `reflection-6/deepseek/RESULT.md`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8994:- **The council** (`reflection-7/challenge-40.md` to `-42.md`, Codex thread rounds 40 to 42) **agreed:**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9004:  - **The rule** (in `reflection-7/second_side_probe.py`):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9024:  - Score: `reflection-7/score-output.txt`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9039:## D653 · 2026-11-17 · Deep council (reflection 8): the state of gate 1 with astra, corrections to D648/D649/D651/D652, and the next step (a $0 audit of a narrow D436 implementation)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9043:  - Claude's own reflection, written first;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9049:  Record: `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/LOG.md`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9121:- **The passage** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/edit.json`, version 5.5):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9295:- **Alex** (2026-11-17), sharing a critique (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-9/alex-critique-2026-11-17.md`, with Claude's check of\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9297:- **Council** (`reflection-9/`):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9298:  - Claude's own reflection, written first (`own-reflection.md`);\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9351:     - Before any council, the earlier reflections on the same question are read and quoted.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9400:- **Council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/`):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10013:  - Claude's reflection, written first (`claude-reflection.md`);\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10223:- **Reflection council K** (a cold read, consensus with Claude's reflection apart from one point):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10233:  - Claude's reflection had proposed taking D198's options to Alex now. Council K: not before the census shows what the hybrid can\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10625:## D708 · 2026-11-21 · Council R (reflection, round 31): a one-pair pilot before the full paid comparison\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10963:  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r48.md:1:# Round 48, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's report)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md:17:  - `claude-r48.md`, Claude's reflection, written first;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round56-brief.md:29:- My own reflection: `claude-r56.md`. Read it after forming your own view.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round50-brief.md:3:You are an independent read-only reviewer. Read the material, then challenge Claude's reflection.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round50-brief.md:10:- **Claude's reflection:** `claude-r49.md`, which argues the repair is not bounded and proposes three options for Alex.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:26:| bridges and `converts` (C8) | a conversion between quantities is computed or estimated as the analyst chooses; code records each computed figure whose inputs measure another quantity, and readers judge it |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round56b-brief.md:11:`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/*.diff`:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r45.md:1:# Claude's reflection before reading Codex's round 45\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round45b-brief.md:3:Thank you. Claude wrote its own reflection before reading yours: `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r45.md`. We agree on\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r56.md:11:3. **Serious — Change both request sentences with the narrower checker fix.** The system asks writers to carry guided growth forward. The schema says the rate can inform an `estimate`, which is a specific figure type, and the header can be read as requiring every calculation path to go through the quarter forecast. A code-only change leaves that tension in place. I would say that a growth rate derived from guidance may inform an estimate or be used in `apply_growth` with the shared quarter’s forecast as the dollar base. The header should require the single forecast wherever the calculation uses that quarter’s **value**. Drop the reflection’s parenthetical that a growth rate is another quantity. The unit alone cannot tell whether the calculation uses it as a benchmark or to recover a second dollar value. Give readers the same distinction. [System text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Schema wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:152) · [Header](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:176) · [Proposed wording](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r56.md:21)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r49.md:1:# Round 49, Claude's reflection after Codex's design review (written before round 50)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r49.md:24:  must satisfy all of them at once. Round 48's reflection already warned that a long conjunction fails by chance even when each part\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r56.md:1:# Round 56, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r56.md:27:   computed from it is another quantity).\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r56.md:32:another quantity. That is relabelling, which S4 never caught when the label differs. The fix does not widen that hole for a USD bn\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md:43:  and reached F4. A rate computed from a quarter's guidance is another quantity. The quarter's value in the calculation is still F8\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
