n   602\t    Quote: Total revenue is expected to be $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\n   603\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   604\t- e2721 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in Q3 FY2027.\n   605\t    Quote: We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.\n   606\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2882, e3264, e3706, e4343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   607\t- e2723 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra ramp.\n   608\t    Quote: Data Center revenue for the second quarter was a record $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago and up 18% sequentially, driven by the ramp of our Blackwell Ultra infrastructure.\n   609\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2668, e2756, e2819, e2842, e3041, e3181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   610\t- e3399 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that Data Center revenue rose from 87.9% of NVIDIA total revenue in fiscal Q2 2026 to 92.5% in fiscal Q2 2027, increasing each quarter in between.\n   611\t    Quote: A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\n   612\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3707; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   613\t- e3401 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion in fiscal Q3 2027 if NVIDIA total revenue reaches its $108.0 billion guidance midpoint and Data Center remains 92.5% of the mix.\n   614\t    Quote: Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\n   615\t- e3406 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA said hyperscale-business growth should reaccelerate in fiscal Q4 2027 as Vera Rubin supply builds.\n   616\t    Quote: And the company said growth in its hyperscale business (sales to the giant cloud computing providers and the biggest consumer internet companies) should reaccelerate in the fiscal fourth quarter as Vera Rubin supply builds.\n   617\t- e4001 [third_party_view; theguardian.com; original source theguardian.com 2026-09-03; from gnews:774c4b3a90a519fc0d3c9024 2026-09-03] Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft are developing their own AI chips to reduce reliance on NVIDIA processors.\n   618\t    Quote: For Nvidia, building up its open source business may help it cushion a demand slowdown from customers such as ⁠Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft, which are developing their own AI chips to cut reliance ​on its costly and ​supply-constrained processors.\n   619\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4038; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   620\t- e4202 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:bbd72d5fbff98d39746e6cb9 2026-09-04] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA could reach $40 billion in revenue per gigawatt of computing capacity installed with Vera Rubin, compared with about $25 billion with Blackwell and $18 billion with Hopper.\n   621\t    Quote: Nvidia used to collect about $18 billion in revenue for every gigawatt of computing capacity it helped install with Hopper. With Blackwell, that figure rose to $25 billion. Kress says that with Vera Rubin, the company can reach $40 billion per gigawatt.\n   622\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2887; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   623\t- e4274 [third_party_view; calcalistech.com; original source calcalistech.com 2026-09-06; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] The article estimates NVIDIA FY2027 revenue at about $400 billion, up about 85% year over year.\n   624\t    Quote: This year, however, revenue is expected to jump to about $400 billion, an increase of about 85% from the previous year.\n   625\t- e4278 [third_party_view; calcalistech.com; original source calcalistech.com 2026-09-06; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] About 92% of NVIDIA revenue comes from data-center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.\n   626\t    Quote: Approximately 92% of Nvidia’s revenue comes from data center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.\n   627\t    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3797; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n   628\t- e4519 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fd039f68d65be67fc1005bcc 2026-09-09] NVIDIA's ACIE business—sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise Data Center revenue—grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.\n   629\t    Quote: ACIE, the sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise side of the data center business, grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor label in ['P','P-v4','P-v8']:\n p=Path('poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22')/label/'item.json'\n it=json.loads(p.read_text()); print(label,it['family'].get('shared'))\nPY\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11345,11372p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_test.py.diff; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_adjudicate.py.diff; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/small_mutants.py.diff\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor label in ['P','P-v4','P-v8']:\n p=Path('poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22')/label/'item.json'\n it=json.loads(p.read_text()); print(label,it['family'].get('shared'))\nPY\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11345,11372p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_test.py.diff; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/blind_adjudicate.py.diff; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/r56b/small_mutants.py.diff\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: can't create temp file for here document: operation not permitted\n 11345\t\n 11346\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n 11347\t\n 11348\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n 11349\t  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n 11350\t  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n 11351\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n 11352\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n 11353\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11354\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n 11355\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n 11356\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n 11357\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n 11358\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n 11359\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n 11360\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n 11361\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\n 11362\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n 11363\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n 11364\t  - Then three steps:\n 11365\t    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n 11366\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n 11367\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n     1\t--- blind_test.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:05\n     2\t+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/blind_test.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:54\n     3\t@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@\n     4\t from pathlib import Path\n     5\t \n     6\t HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n     7\t sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n     8\t sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n     9\t import calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\n    10\t@@ -173,8 +173,8 @@\n    11\t - part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n    12\t   includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\n    13\t - two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n    14\t-  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n    15\t-  calculation (a ruling).\n    16\t+  guidance and used as a stated benchmark for an estimate, or applied (apply_growth) to a base built on the quarter's one forecast\n    17\t+  figure, is not a second value, when that figure supplies the quarter's value in the calculation (a ruling).\n    18\t - own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n    19\t   estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n    20\t   applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n     1\t--- blind_adjudicate.py\t2026-11-22 19:58:24\n     2\t+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/blind_adjudicate.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:54\n     3\t@@ -23,8 +23,8 @@\n     4\t - part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n     5\t   includes it.\n     6\t - two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n     7\t-  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n     8\t-  calculation (a ruling).\n     9\t+  guidance and used as a stated benchmark for an estimate, or applied (apply_growth) to a base built on the quarter's one forecast\n    10\t+  figure, is not a second value, when that figure supplies the quarter's value in the calculation (a ruling).\n    11\t - own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n    12\t   estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n    13\t   applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n     1\t--- small_mutants.py\t2026-11-22 19:42:29\n     2\t+++ /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/s4tree/small_mutants.py\t2026-11-22 20:11:04\n     3\t@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n     4\t from pathlib import Path\n     5\t \n     6\t HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n     7\t M = [\n     8\t     ('S1 value', \"            ok = _same(f.get('value'), parsed['value'])\\n\", \"            ok = True\\n\"),\n     9\t     ('S1 qualifier', \"        if q not in written:\\n\", \"        if False:\\n\"),\n    10\t@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@\n    11\t     ('S4 two forecasts', \"        if len(ids) > 1:\\n            errors.append(('S4'\", \"        if False:\\n            errors.append(('S4'\"),\n    12\t     ('S4 adopted only', \"        if k not in keys:\\n            tops.add(fid)\", \"        if True:\\n            tops.add(fid)\"),\n    13\t     ('S4 bypass', \"            if bypass:\\n\", \"            if False:\\n\"),\n    14\t+    ('S4 benchmark exemption [D742]', \"and node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0]):\", \"and False:\"),\n    15\t+    ('S4 exemption needs the forecast as base [D742]', \"and node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0]):\", \":\"),\n    16\t     ('S5 estimate under reference', \"            if any(figs[g]['kind'] == 'estimate' for g in chain):\", \"            if False:\"),\n    17\t     ('S5 forecast under reference', \"            elif any(figs[g]['basis'] == 'forecast' for g in chain):\", \"            elif False:\"),\n    18\t     ('S5 outside source', \"            elif not any(figs[g]['kind'] == 'source' and figs[g]['basis'] in EXTERNAL for g in chain):\", \"            elif False:\"),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The narrowed check looks for the adopted forecast in the starting amount, then skips the entire growth-rate calculation. I’m testing whether that can hide a return to the guidance number, and whether equivalent arithmetic gets refused."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import copy, json, sys, types, re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrepo = Path.cwd()\nroot = repo / '\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\''\nsys.path[:0] = [str(root), str(repo / '\\\\''src'\\\\'')]\nimport calc_small as current\nimport render_v13 as render\nfrom hivemind import model\n\ndef patched(name):\n    lines = (root/name).read_text().splitlines(True)\n    diff = (root/'\\\\''r56b'\\\\''/(name+'\\\\''.diff'\\\\'')).read_text().splitlines(True)[2:]\n    offset, index = 0, 0\n    while index < len(diff):\n        at = int(re.match(r'\\\\''@@ -(\\\\d+)'\\\\'', diff[index]).group(1)) - 1 + offset\n        index += 1\n        before, after = [], []\n        while index < len(diff) and not diff[index].startswith('\\\\''@@'\\\\''):\n            line = diff[index]\n            if line[0] in '\\\\'' -'\\\\'': before.append(line[1:])\n            if line[0] in '\\\\'' +'\\\\'': after.append(line[1:])\n            index += 1\n        assert lines[at:at+len(before)] == before, (name, at)\n        lines[at:at+len(before)] = after\n        offset += len(after)-len(before)\n    return '\\\\'''\\\\''.join(lines)\n\ndef load(name, src, path):\n    module = types.ModuleType(name)\n    module.__file__ = str(root/path)\n    exec(compile(src, module.__file__, '\\\\''exec'\\\\''), module.__dict__)\n    return module\n\nfix_src = patched('\\\\''calc_small.py'\\\\'')\nfix = load('\\\\''fix'\\\\'', fix_src, '\\\\''calc_small.py'\\\\'')\nblanket = load('\\\\''blanket'\\\\'', (root/'\\\\''s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt'\\\\'').read_text(), '\\\\''s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt'\\\\'')\nnew_render = load('\\\\''new_render'\\\\'', patched('\\\\''render_v13.py'\\\\''), '\\\\''render_v13.py'\\\\'')\ncases = load('\\\\''new_cases'\\\\'', patched('\\\\''small_cases.py'\\\\''), '\\\\''small_cases.py'\\\\'')\nsmall_mutants = load('\\\\''new_mutants'\\\\'', patched('\\\\''small_mutants.py'\\\\''), '\\\\''small_mutants.py'\\\\'')\nmutants = {'\\\\''disabled'\\\\'': '\\\\''S4 benchmark exemption [D742]'\\\\'', '\\\\''no base'\\\\'': '\\\\''S4 exemption needs the forecast as base [D742]'\\\\'', '\\\\''no bypass'\\\\'': '\\\\''S4 bypass'\\\\''}\nmods = {'\\\\''current'\\\\'':current, '\\\\''blanket'\\\\'':blanket, '\\\\''narrow'\\\\'':fix}\nfor lab,name in mutants.items():\n    _,old,new = next(m for m in small_mutants.M if m[0] == name)\n    assert fix_src.count(old)==1\n    mods[lab] = load(lab,fix_src.replace(old,new),'\\\\''calc_small.py'\\\\'')\nat = '\\\\''node[0] in _beneath_inputs(figs, ins[0])'\\\\''\nmods['\\\\''direct only'\\\\''] = load('\\\\''direct'\\\\'',fix_src.replace(at,'\\\\''node[0] == ins[0]'\\\\''),'\\\\''calc_small.py'\\\\'')\nassert fix_src.count(at) == 1\n\ndef status(m,a,f,p,s):\n    e = model.check_schema(a,s)\n    if e: return '\\\\''schema'\\\\'', e, {}, []\n    calc = m.from_answer(a,f)\n    r = m.check(f,p,calc)\n    return m.publish_decision(f,calc,r),r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''],r['\\\\''published'\\\\''],r['\\\\''recorded'\\\\'']\n\nfor label,m in mods.items():\n    fails = []\n    for group,name,expect,rec,build in cases.CASES:\n        a,f=build()\n        result = status(m,a,f,cases.PASSAGES,new_render.v13s_schema(sorted(f['\\\\''members'\\\\'']),cases.EVIDENCE, []))\n        flag = result[0] if result[0]=='\\\\''schema'\\\\'' else '\\\\'','\\\\''.join(sorted({c for c,_ in result[1]})) or '\\\\''pass'\\\\''\n        ok = flag==expect\n        if ok and name in cases.MESSAGES:\n            ok = any(cases.MESSAGES[name] in d for _,d in result[1])\n        if ok and rec:\n            ok = any(r['\\\\''type'\\\\'']==rec for r in result[3])\n        if not ok: fails.append((name,flag,result[1][:3]))\n    print(label, len(cases.CASES)-len(fails), '\\\\''/'\\\\'', len(cases.CASES))\n    for x in fails: print('\\\\'' '\\\\'',x)\n\ndata_dir = repo/'\\\\''poc/data'\\\\''\nimport blind_test as bt\ncompared = []\nfor folder in ['\\\\''judging-v13s-blind-2026-11-22'\\\\'','\\\\''judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22'\\\\'']:\n    for name in bt.CASES:\n        label = data_dir / folder / name\n        it = json.loads((label / '\\\\''item.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n        for writer in bt.WRITERS:\n            a=bt.first_json((label/'\\\\''answers'\\\\''/f'\\\\''{writer}.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n            args = (a,it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],it['\\\\''schema'\\\\''])\n            before,after = [status(mod,*args) for mod in [current,fix]]\n            assert before[0] \"'!= '\"'\\\\''schema'\\\\'' and after[0] \"'!= '\"'\\\\''schema'\\\\''\n            compared.append((folder,name,writer,before[:2],after[:2]))\nprint('\\\\''census:'\\\\'',len(compared),[r for r in compared if r[-2]\"'!=r[-1]])\ndef saved(case='\"'\\\\''P-v4'\\\\''):\n    p=data_dir/'\\\\''judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22'\\\\''/case\n    it=json.loads((p/'\\\\''item.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n    a=bt.first_json((p/'\\\\''answers/claude.json'\\\\'').read_text())\n    return a,it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],it['\\\\''schema'\\\\'']\nprint('\\\\''shared:'\\\\'',[(case,saved(case)[1]['\\\\''shared'\\\\'']) for case in ['\\\\''P'\\\\'','\\\\''P-v4'\\\\'','\\\\''P-v8'\\\\'']])\n\nF,W,fig=cases.F,cases.W,cases.fig\ndef revalue(a):\n    figs={x['\\\\''id'\\\\'']:x for x in a['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']}\n    calculated=current.evaluate(figs)\n    for row in figs.values():\n        if row['\\\\''kind'\\\\'']\"'!='\"'\\\\''computed'\\\\'': continue\n        lo,hi=calculated[row['\\\\''id'\\\\'']]\n        row.update(value=None if lo\"'!=hi else lo,low=lo if lo!=hi else None,high=hi if lo!=hi else None)\ndef set_calc(a,fid,op,ins):\n    fig(a,fid).update(kind='\"'\\\\''computed'\\\\'',operation=op,inputs=ins,rests_on=None,basis_text=None)\ndef add_calc(a,id,what,basis,unit,operation,inputs):\n    a['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(F(id,what,'\\\\''computed'\\\\'',basis,unit,value=0,operation=operation,inputs=inputs))\ndef probe(name,args):\n    a,f,p,s=args\n    revalue(a)\n    print(name,[(m,status(mod,a,f,p,s)[:3]) for m,mod in mods.items() if m in ['\\\\''current'\\\\'','\\\\''narrow'\\\\'','\\\\''blanket'\\\\'']])\n    print('\\\\''  duplicate marks:'\\\\'',[r for r in status(fix,a,f,p,s)[3] if r['\\\\''type'\\\\'']=='\\\\''one quantity, several figures'\\\\''])\nfor is_range in [False,True]:\n    args=saved(); a=args[0]\n    if is_range: fig(a,'\\\\''F4'\\\\'').update(value=None,low=105.84,high=110.16)\n    fig(a,'\\\\''F9'\\\\'').update(what=W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q3'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''revenue change from own forecast to guidance'\\\\''), inputs=['\\\\''F8'\\\\'','\\\\''F4'\\\\''])\n    q4rate=F('\\\\''R'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q4'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''revenue sequential growth'\\\\''),'\\\\''estimate'\\\\'','\\\\''forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''%'\\\\'',value=12.,basis_text='\\\\''Carry the guided sequential pace forward alongside the expected Q4 ramp.'\\\\'')\n    a['\\\\''figures'\\\\''].append(q4rate)\n    add_calc(a,'\\\\''BASE'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q4'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''revenue starting run-rate'\\\\''),'\\\\''forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''apply_growth'\\\\'',['\\\\''F8'\\\\'','\\\\''F9'\\\\''])\n    set_calc(a,'\\\\''F10'\\\\'','\\\\''apply_growth'\\\\'',['\\\\''BASE'\\\\'','\\\\''R'\\\\''])\n    a['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''reasons'\\\\'']='\\\\''Count my Q3 estimate in full-year revenue but reset the Q4 starting run-rate towards guidance before adding 12% for Q4.'\\\\''\n    probe('\\\\''guidance reset range='\\\\''+str(is_range),args)\n\nargs=saved(); a=args[0]\nfig(a,'\\\\''F9'\\\\'').update(unit='\\\\''x'\\\\'',inputs=['\\\\''F4'\\\\'','\\\\''F2'\\\\''],operation='\\\\''ratio'\\\\'')\nset_calc(a,'\\\\''F10'\\\\'','\\\\''product'\\\\'',['\\\\''F8'\\\\'','\\\\''F9'\\\\''])\nprobe('\\\\''equivalent multiplier'\\\\'',args)\n\nargs=saved(); a=args[0]\na